{
  "requirement": "`ValidationContext::inspection()` exposes the execution's `InspectionContext`.\nThe ask builder passes that context to `Agent::run`. The supplied `ToolAgent`\nimplements graph-node reads, outgoing-edge queries, and delivery recording by\ndelegating to that same context's operations.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "Every structural obligation in `requirements.sdk.graph.context-tools.shared_context` is met by the sources I reviewed. The requirement is structural, so I found no runtime outcome that needs test evidence.\n\n- **`ValidationContext::inspection()` exposes the execution's `InspectionContext`.**\n  - `crates/habeas-sdk/src/procedure.rs#impl[ValidationContext<'d, D>]#1/fn[inspection]` returns `&self.inspection`.\n  - That field is the `InspectionContext<'d, D>` held by `struct[ValidationContext]`. `fn[configured]` builds it with `InspectionContext::new(graph)`.\n- **The ask builder passes that context to `Agent::run`.**\n  - `crates/habeas-sdk/src/procedure.rs#impl[Ask<'a, 'd, D, R, P>]#2/fn[execute]` calls `agent.run(request, &self.ctx.inspection)`.\n  - It also uses the same `self.ctx.inspection` for `prepare_edges`, `prepare_read` and `graph()` while it prepares the inputs.\n  - `trait[Agent]/fn[run]` takes `inspection: &'a InspectionContext<'_, D>`, so the context reaches the agent.\n- **`ToolAgent` delegates to that same context's operations.**\n  - `crates/habeas-sdk/src/agent/tools.rs#impl[ToolAgent<P, T>/Agent<D>]/fn[run]` stores the received `inspection` reference in `GraphSession`. `struct[GraphSession]` holds `inspection: &'a InspectionContext<'d, D>`.\n  - Graph-node reads: `impl[GraphSession<'_, '_, D>/Conversation]/fn[dispatch]` handles `read_node` with `self.inspection.prepare_read` and `self.inspection.graph().format_node_content`.\n  - Outgoing-edge queries: the same `dispatch` handles `outgoing_edges` with `self.inspection.prepare_edges` and `graph().node_path`.\n  - Delivery recording: `impl[GraphSession<'_, '_, D>/Conversation]/fn[delivered]` drains the pending observations. It calls `self.inspection.observe_read` for `Dependency::Node` and `self.inspection.observe_edges` for `Dependency::OutgoingEdges`.\n\nNo `{fixme}` acknowledgments apply, and I found no conflicting or missing structural element.",
